{"seq":18,"trial_id":"v03-opus-dev-2026-10/hermes-opus-gbrain-told-scoped-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r5","wall_ts":"2026-11-01T10:23:36.201Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"df42a4403f1e4294994483b2a3f3e9f13b05485ff93130ef218262e766ab1099","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","text":"Hi Dana. I went through every one of Moss's notes you can see (the North and Central digests in the team folders). Two ticket numbers relate to Quarrendon Freight Lines:\n\n- #PD-4492: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025 because gatehouse kiosk SMS bay assignments weren't reaching drivers at Dock Doors 14-18 in Eau Claire. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that it was fixed. The same note also lists it as a 6 Oct triage item: archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n- #4419: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing.\n\nIn Moss's other notes:\n- The 9/14 North pipeline digest covers QFL but has no ticket number.\n- The 3/23 renewal check-in has no ticket number.\n- #4409, #4412 and FR-882 in the Central handoffs digest belong to Central accounts (Marrow), not QFL.\n- Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" is about a different company that isn't a customer, and Moss didn't write it.\n\nOne more you might want, though it isn't from Moss: the QFL account page lists ticket #4912, which is still open with support. It covers lag on the Gate_Dwell_Daily report for Bay 14 check-ins at the Superior yard."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":19,"trial_id":"v03-opus-dev-2026-10/hermes-opus-gbrain-told-scoped-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r5","wall_ts":"2026-11-01T10:23:41.918Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"e6e3453de5d5afc27b7f1881af3137bcde5f4b6b91d51030800f429e6c6a681e","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in the Moss notes you can see. I've sent you the list with sources in our DM.\n\n1. #PD-4492, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at Eau Claire Dock Doors 14–18 weren't getting their bay assignments by text when they checked in at the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that it was fixed.\n2. #4419, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). The gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it went to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nThe rest of Moss's notes:\n- The 9/14 North pipeline digest and the 3/23 renewal check-in mention Quarrendon Freight Lines but give no ticket numbers.\n- The ticket numbers in the Central handoffs digest (#4409, #4412 and FR-882) belong to Central accounts.\n- Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" is about a different company that isn't a customer, and Moss didn't write it.\n\nThe Quarrendon Freight Lines account page also lists ticket #4912. It isn't from Moss's notes, so I listed it separately in case you want it. It's still open with support, for lag on the Gate_Dwell_Daily report for Bay 14 check-ins at the Superior yard."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
